n elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement II is false, while statements I and III are true." 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322205 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322206 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322207 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322208 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322209 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1041 "selection" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322206 13194139534952 true] [17592186322204 1110 #uuid "57eacdce-d0b1-503a-bc21-6b75907396a5" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322205 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534952 true] [17592186322205 1111 #uuid "0c4ebe63-1468-518b-a60c-d24200234fee" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322206 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534952 true] [17592186322206 1111 #uuid "3c919a80-b519-51d5-89e1-b3492a49f913" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322207 1034 "III only" 13194139534952 true] [17592186322207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 1319413953